  "problem": "Census product/vintage/geography metadata could collapse ACS 5-year, ACS 1-year and time-series identities, infer observation period from vintage, place a Census key in evidence URLs, or emit a sample recipe before required inputs and a secret-provider key were present.",
  "resulting_behavior": "bindCensusProducts keeps ACSST5Y2023, ACSST1Y2023 and BDSTIMESERIES distinct. Vintage is not an observation period. Variables/geography/groups/examples links bind to exact catalog entries over HTTPS. A Census key is received only through secretProvider.getSecret and never appears in evidence URLs, logs or query redaction. Missing keys produce a documented access step. Offline tests run with no secret. Keyless Missing Key HTML remains authentication-required and not JSON success. Pennsylvania state:42 uses S0101_C01_001E and documented geography predicates. Labels/concepts are not definitions. Sample recipes are withheld until required inputs including the key are present. Live fetch is forbidden.",
